   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 54 of the laws of 1938 authorizing Exempt Firemen's\nBenevolent Association of Hastings on the Hudson, Inc., to collect, receive\nand use taxes required to be paid pursuant to the insurance law upon premiums\non policies of fire insurance on property in the village of Hastings on the\nHudson, New York, or other territory served by the fire department thereof, in\nrelation to the use of taxes collected",
    "basePrintNo": "S9306",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S9306-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1, Chap 54 of 1938",
    "lawSection": "Firefighters' Benevolent Association",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9306\n\nSPONSOR: STEWART-COUSINS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 54 of the laws of 1938 authorizing Exempt Fire-\nmen's Benevolent Association of Hastings on the Hudson, Inc., to\ncollect, receive and use taxes required to be paid pursuant to the\ninsurance law upon premiums on policies of fire insurance on property in\nthe village of Hastings on the Hudson, New York, or other territory\nserved by the fire department thereof, in relation to the use of taxes\ncollected\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to update the name of the Exempt Firefight-\ners' Benevolent Association of Hastings-on-Hudson, Inc. in existing law,\nas well as update the purposes and duties of the Association. Addi-\ntionally, the bill updates the way funds received by the Association\nfrom foreign fire insurance companies are collected and distributed, and\nthe way funds received by the Association from the Superintendent of\nFinancial Services of the State of New York are spent, to comply with\nmodem NY Insurance Law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends existing law to reflect the current name of\nthe Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Association of Hastings-on-Hudson,\nInc., and states the most up-to-date purposes of the Association.\n\nAdditionally, this section amends existing law to state that a percent-\nage of the foreign fire insurance premium taxes collected by the Associ-\nation must go to the Treasure of the Firefighters' Association of the\nState of New York, as required by New York Insurance Law, and the Asso-\nciation must use the remaining funds only to achieve its stated\npurposes.\n\nFinally, this section amends existing law to state that the Exempt Fire-\nfighters' Benevolent Association of Hastings-on-Hudson, Inc. must use\nany funds received from the Superintendent of Financial Services of the\nState of New York, as required by New York Insurance Law, only to\nachieve its stated purposes.\n\nSection 2 is the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATIONf\n\nThis bill provides necessary amendments to existing law to ensure that\nall language relating to the Exempt Firefighters' Benevolent Association\nof Hastings-on-Hudson, Inc. and New York Insurance Laws is up to date.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and shall apply to taxes due on\npremiums received on and after January 1, 2025.\n",
